[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterodimer composed of a catalytic subunit CDK5 and a regulatory subunit CDK5R1 (p25) and macromolecular complex composed of at least CDK5, CDK5R1 (p35) and CDK5RAP1 or CDK5RAP2 or CDK5RAP3. Only the heterodimer shows kinase activity. Under neurotoxic stress and neuronal injury conditions, p35 is cleaved by calpain to generate p25 that hyperactivates CDK5, that becomes functionally disabled and often toxic. Found in a trimolecular complex with CABLES1 and ABL1. Interacts with CABLES1 and CABLES2 (By similarity). Interacts with AATK and GSTP1. Binds to HDAC1 when in complex with p25. Interaction with myristoylation p35 promotes CDK5 association with membranes. Both isoforms 1 and 2 interacts with beta-catenin/CTNNB1. Interacts with delta-catenin/CTNND2 and APEX1. Interacts with P53/TP53 in neurons. Interacts with EPHA4; may mediate the activation of NGEF by EPHA4. Interacts with PTK2/FAK1 (By similarity). The complex p35/CDK5 interacts with CLOCK. Interacts with HTR6 (By similarity)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q00535-2","name":"2","synonyms":["CDK5-SV"],"notes":[],"length":260,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000297518.4"],"refseq":["NM_001164410.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001157882.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,104],[105,137,156]],"edits":[{"start":105,"end":136,"original":"SFLFQLLKGLGFCHSRNVLHRDLKPQNLLINR","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":32,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":32,"foldedMissing":32,"features":[[0,32,0],[7,1,0]],"interfaces":{"CABLES1":[5,0,37],"CABLES2":[5,0,40],"CCNA1":[7,0,56],"CCNB1":[5,0,44],"CCNB2":[6,0,52],"CCNB3":[6,0,48],"CCNC":[4,0,26],"CCNE1":[4,0,41],"CCNE2":[4,0,37],"CCNI":[6,0,50],"CCNI2":[4,0,40],"CCNO":[4,0,33],"CCNP":[6,0,34],"CDK5R1":[3,0,36],"CNPPD1":[4,0,47],"SPDYA":[1,0,31],"SPDYE4":[4,0,31]},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q00535-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q00535-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":87.5,"plddt":[[50,1],[70,1],[90,7],[70,3],[50,3